Now I'll compile my research findings. Let me create a comprehensive summary with paths and concrete recommendations.

## Research Findings: Canvas RCE Locale & Save Persistence

### Current Architecture Summary

**Three deployment modes:**
1. **Docs iframe embed** (`/guide/canvas-rce`) - NO header, always English
2. **Standalone app** (`/tools/canvas-rce/` when opened directly) - HAS shell header with locale picker
3. **Scaffolded local project** - `npx create-pantoken-app canvas-theme-editor` - HAS shell header with locale picker

---

## 1. Build & Iframe Embedding Structure

**Build pipeline:**
- [build-canvas-rce.ts](docs/scripts/build-canvas-rce.ts#L28-L33): Hardcoded `locale: "en"` at scaffold time
  ```typescript
  await scaffoldProject("canvas-theme-editor", renderDir, {
    locale: "en",  // ← Always English, never uses docs locale
    cdn: "jsdelivr",
    theme: "rebrand",
    mode: "light",
    packageManager: "npm",
  });
  ```
- Built output placed at `docs/public/tools/canvas-rce/` (served at `/tools/canvas-rce/`)

**Vue embed component:**
- [CanvasRcePage.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CanvasRcePage.vue#L20-L27):
  ```typescript
  const iframeSrc = computed(() =>
    withBase(`/tools/canvas-rce/index.html${import.meta.env.DEV ? `?t=${Date.now()}` : ""}`),
  );
  ```
  - Dev uses cache-bust `?t=` timestamp param
  - Production uses plain URL (hashed by Vite)
  - **NO `?locale=` param currently passed**
  - iframe size synced via postMessage of `"pantoken:canvas-rce:height"`

**Static base path handling:**
- [build-canvas-rce.ts](docs/scripts/build-canvas-rce.ts#L93): `base: "/tools/canvas-rce/"`
- Means all relative asset URLs (CSS, JS, icon pickers) are relative to `/tools/canvas-rce/`, not site root

---

## 2. Standalone Shell Header (When NOT embedded)

**Detection & rendering:**
- [main.ts.tmpl:281-282](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L281-L282): 
  ```typescript
  function setupStandaloneAppShell(): void {
    if (window.self !== window.top || document.getElementById("canvas-rce-shell")) return;
  ```
  - Checks `window.self !== window.top` → only renders in standalone (not iframe)
  - Condition: `window.self === window.top`

**Shell includes:**
- [main.ts.tmpl:317-378](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L317-L378): Locale menu with all available locales
- [main.ts.tmpl:381-521](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L381-L521): Theme/color picker menu

**Styling:**
- [app.css:29-44](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.css#L29-L44): Body flex layout changes when shell enabled
  ```css
  body.canvas-rce-shell-enabled {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 0;
  }
  ```

---

## 3. Locale Persistence Mechanism (Standalone Only)

**Storage key:**
- [main.ts.tmpl:545](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L545): 
  ```typescript
  const LOCALE_STORAGE_KEY = "pantoken-canvas-theme-editor-locale";
  ```

**Locale flow:**
1. **Load at startup** [main.ts.tmpl:548-551](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L548-L551):
   ```typescript
   function loadLocale(): string {
     try {
       return localStorage.getItem(LOCALE_STORAGE_KEY) || "en";
     } catch {
       return "en";
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Apply to document** [main.ts.tmpl:553-557](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L553-L557):
   ```typescript
   const activeLocale = loadLocale();
   const activeStrings = { ...STRINGS, ...LOCALE_STRINGS[activeLocale] };
   document.documentElement.lang = activeLocale;
   document.documentElement.dir = LOCALE_DIRS[activeLocale] ?? "ltr";
   ```

3. **Persist on user selection** [main.ts.tmpl:360-372](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L360-L372):
   ```typescript
   option.addEventListener("click", () => {
     if (locale === document.documentElement.lang) {
       localeMenu.removeAttribute("open");
       return;
     }
     try {
       localStorage.setItem(LOCALE_STORAGE_KEY, locale);
     } catch {
       // Private mode
     }
     // Reload app with new locale strings
     window.location.reload();
   });
   ```

**Key observation:** Changing locale triggers full `window.location.reload()` to re-initialize with new strings and directionality. This is NOT iframe-compatible (docs parent can't reload the iframe this way).

---

## 4. Save & Content Persistence Mechanisms

### Two Independent Layers:

**Layer 1: `pantoken_save` Plugin (Named Presets)**
- [plugins/tinymce/save/src/index.ts:1-30](plugins/tinymce/save/src/index.ts#L1-L30):
  ```typescript
  export const SAVE_PLUGIN_NAME = "pantoken_save";
  export const SAVE_STORAGE_KEY = "pantoken-tinymce-save-presets";
  ```
- Stores **named preset objects** (save/open/delete/export/import UI)
- Used in toolbar: [main.ts.tmpl:1793](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L1793)
  ```typescript
  plugins: "pantoken pantoken_save ... autosave fullscreen ..."
  toolbar: `${SAVE_TOOLBAR_NAME} undo redo ...`
  ```
- Separate from TinyMCE autosave (different storage key)
- Captures full state: `captureCanvasThemePreset()` [main.ts.tmpl:1125-1135](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L1125-L1135)

**Layer 2: TinyMCE `autosave` Plugin (Draft Recovery)**
- [main.ts.tmpl:1815-1819](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L1815-L1819):
  ```typescript
  autosave_ask_before_unload: true,
  autosave_interval: "30s",
  autosave_retention: "30m",
  autosave_restore_when_empty: false,
  ```
- Persists editor HTML content ONLY to localStorage every 30s
- Shows "unsaved changes" warning on page navigation (`autosave_ask_before_unload`)
- Stores under TinyMCE's default key (separate from `pantoken_save`)
- `autosave_restore_when_empty: false` → doesn't auto-restore if user opens new document

### Content Preservation During Navigation:

**For scaffold header reload (standalone):**
- [main.ts.tmpl:1510-1513](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L1510-L1513):
  ```typescript
  window.addEventListener("beforeunload", () => {
    if (previewPopupCloseTimer !== undefined) window.clearInterval(previewPopupCloseTimer);
    previewPopup?.close();
  });
  ```
  - Only closes popup, doesn't prevent navigation
  - TinyMCE `autosave` plugin handles the "unsaved changes" warning

**For docs parent locale change (iframe case):**
- **Current problem:** No mechanism exists
- When parent reloads iframe (e.g., via new `?locale=hu` param), the iframe's `beforeunload` fires but autosave doesn't know about parent navigation
- Content would be preserved in browser autosave, but only if user didn't close the tab

---

## 5. URL Parameter Strategy (Not Currently Implemented)

**Current iframe src construction:**
- [CanvasRcePage.vue:20-27](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CanvasRcePage.vue#L20-L27):
  ```typescript
  const iframeSrc = computed(() =>
    withBase(`/tools/canvas-rce/index.html${import.meta.env.DEV ? `?t=${Date.now()}` : ""}`),
  );
  ```

**Option 1: Add `?locale=` to iframe src (Minimal, Recommended)**
```typescript
const iframeSrc = computed(() => {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  params.set("locale", docsLocale); // Use computed docs locale
  if (import.meta.env.DEV) params.set("t", Date.now().toString());
  return withBase(`/tools/canvas-rce/index.html?${params.toString()}`);
});
```

**In canvas-theme-editor app** (to be added):
- Read URL param early: `new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("locale")`
- **Do NOT** use for localStorage (that would override user's standalone preference)
- Only use when in iframe mode: `window.self !== window.top`

**Locale detection precedence (iframe mode):**
1. URL param `?locale=` (docs parent controls)
2. Browser language as fallback
3. Default "en"

**Locale detection precedence (standalone mode):**
1. localStorage `"pantoken-canvas-theme-editor-locale"` (user's persisted choice)
2. Initial HTML `lang` attribute (build-time scaffold locale)
3. Browser language
4. Default "en"

---

## 6. Docs Locale Switching & Iframe

**Current VitePress i18n setup:**
- [docs/.vitepress/i18n.ts:70-75](docs/.vitepress/i18n.ts#L70-L75): Defines all docs locales
- [docs/.vitepress/theme/canvas-rce.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/canvas-rce.ts): Per-locale string overrides for page chrome (NOT the embedded editor)

**Problem:** When docs locale changes (user clicks language switcher), Vue route changes but iframe src doesn't update → iframe stays on English.

**Solution:** 
- Docs component must recompute iframe URL when docs locale changes
- CanvasRcePage.vue currently has no access to docs locale
- Need to pass `useData().locale` from VitePress to iframe src

**Implementation sketch:**
```typescript
// In CanvasRcePage.vue
import { useData } from "vitepress";
const { locale } = useData();
const iframeSrc = computed(() => {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  params.set("locale", locale.value);
  if (import.meta.env.DEV) params.set("t", Date.now().toString());
  return withBase(`/tools/canvas-rce/index.html?${params.toString()}`);
});
```

**In embedded app** (main.ts.tmpl):
```typescript
// Early in app init, before DOM rendering
const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
const urlLocale = urlParams.get("locale");
const isEmbedded = window.self !== window.top;

const activeLocale = isEmbedded && urlLocale ? urlLocale : loadLocale();
// ... rest of locale setup
```

---

## 7. Security Considerations

**URL parameter validation:**
- Locale must be validated against `LOCALES` from `@pantoken/web-components`
- [docs/.vitepress/i18n.ts:6-7](docs/.vitepress/i18n.ts#L6-L7): 
  ```typescript
  import { LOCALES } from "@pantoken/web-components";
  export const NON_ROOT_LOCALES = Object.keys(LOCALES).filter((key) => key !== "en");
  ```
- Recommended: Only accept if in `["en", ...NON_ROOT_LOCALES]`
- No serialization risk (plain BCP47 tag, no JSON, no script)

**localStorage access:**
- Both mechanisms wrap in try-catch for private mode
- No sensitive data stored (only UI preferences and editor content)
- [main.ts.tmpl:548-551](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L548-L551): Already handles gracefully

**Cache-busting:**
- Dev: timestamp param (`?t=`) ensures fresh fetch each load
- Production: Vite hashing on filename handles cache invalidation
- Adding `?locale=` param adds dimension but doesn't break existing cache strategy (query params are part of cache key)

---

## 8. Testing Needs

**Unit tests for locale detection:**
```typescript
// Test URL param takes precedence in iframe mode
const locale = getLocale(true, "hu", undefined); // isEmbedded, urlParam, stored
expect(locale).toBe("hu");

// Test stored value takes precedence in standalone mode
const locale = getLocale(false, "hu", "fr"); // isEmbedded=false, urlParam, stored
expect(locale).toBe("fr");
```

**Integration tests:**
- [ ] Embedded iframe receives `?locale=X` and renders in that language
- [ ] Docs locale change triggers iframe reload with new `?locale=` param
- [ ] Standalone app loads localStorage choice on init
- [ ] Standalone locale picker persists to localStorage and reloads
- [ ] Autosave survives iframe navigation (check if draft recovers)
- [ ] Named presets (`pantoken_save`) survive iframe locale change

**Checkpoint history:**
- Session memory already contains detailed research: [/memories/session/canvas-theme-editor-locale-research.md](file:///memories/session/canvas-theme-editor-locale-research.md)
- No prior checkpoint commits found for this specific feature

---

## 9. Concrete Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Add URL locale detection to embedded app
**File:** [packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L545-L560)

Replace locale loading logic with:
```typescript
const LOCALE_STORAGE_KEY = "pantoken-canvas-theme-editor-locale";

function loadLocale(): string {
  const isEmbedded = window.self !== window.top;
  const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
  const urlLocale = urlParams.get("locale");

  // URL param precedence in iframe; localStorage precedence standalone
  if (isEmbedded && urlLocale) {
    const validLocales = ["en", ...Object.keys(LOCALE_STRINGS).sort()];
    if (validLocales.includes(urlLocale)) return urlLocale;
  }

  try {
    const stored = localStorage.getItem(LOCALE_STORAGE_KEY);
    if (stored) return stored;
  } catch {
    // Private mode
  }

  return "en";
}
```

### Step 2: Update docs iframe component
**File:** [docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CanvasRcePage.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CanvasRcePage.vue#L5-L27)

```typescript
import { computed, onBeforeUnmount, onMounted, ref } from "vue";
import { useData, withBase } from "vitepress";
import { CANVAS_RCE_DEFAULTS, CANVAS_RCE_HEIGHT_MESSAGE } from "../canvas-rce";

const { theme, locale } = useData();
const t = computed(() => ({
  ...CANVAS_RCE_DEFAULTS,
  ...((theme.value as Record<string, unknown>).canvasRce as object),
}));

const iframeSrc = computed(() => {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  // Pass docs locale to embedded app
  params.set("locale", locale.value);
  if (import.meta.env.DEV) params.set("t", Date.now().toString());
  return withBase(`/tools/canvas-rce/index.html?${params.toString()}`);
});
// ... rest unchanged
```

### Step 3: Add validation tests
**File:** [packages/scaffold/tests/index.test.ts](packages/scaffold/tests/index.test.ts)

Add tests for:
- URL param validation against LOCALES
- Embedded vs standalone locale precedence
- RTL/LTR directionality per locale

### Step 4: Update integration test for iframe
**File:** Check existing iframe height tests; add locale param verification

---

## Summary Table

| Aspect | Current State | Issue | Recommendation |
|--------|---------------|-------|-----------------|
| **Embedded iframe locale** | Hardcoded English | Docs locale changes don't update iframe | Add `?locale=` param to iframe src |
| **Standalone shell locale** | localStorage + reload | Works as-is | Keep as-is; URL param ignored in standalone |
| **Autosave draft recovery** | Per-content 30s interval | No issue | Document that localStorage is separate from named presets |
| **Named presets** | `pantoken_save` plugin | Survive navigation | Verify localStorage keys don't conflict |
| **Content during locale switch** | Autosave preserves | Works if user accepts warning | Add integration test |
| **Cache-busting** | Dev: timestamp, Prod: hashing | No conflict with `?locale=` | Keep current strategy |
| **Security** | Try-catch wrappers | No data injection risk | Validate locale string against LOCALES |

---

**All paths linked above for direct navigation to implementation sites.**

